    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d982">

                <pb facs="0907" n="897" xml:id="pg897"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.111/508: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Paxton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-08T16:00:00+09:00">October 8, 1941—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 9—11:13 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>70. It is reported that officials of Governments which have recognized the Wang
                        régime<anchor n="69" xml:id="d982-f1"/> are soon to receive passes
                    indefinitely valid for travel anywhere in Japanese occupied territory. Baggage
                    inspection is to be waived for them.</p>
                <p>Travel passes are to be issued to non-official nationals of these countries
                    indefinitely valid for specified areas permitting transportation of any articles
                    not prohibited in the case of Japanese subjects.</p>
                <p>No change in the treatment accorded Americans or nationals of other
                    non-recognizing Governments as regards travel in this area has been reported or
                    seems to be in contemplation as yet.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department, repeated to Chungking, Peiping and Shanghai, by mail to
                    Tokyo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paxton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d982-f1" n="69" xml:id="d982-f1-content">
                <p>Japanese-sponsored “government” at Nanking.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
